<title>UK: UK's Zeneca shares up in technical bounce.</title>
<headline>UK's Zeneca shares up in technical bounce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British drugs firm Zeneca Group Plc on Thursday rose 20-1/2 pence to 1,866 in a technical bounce following recent underperformance.</p>
<p>&quot;They have been bombed out in the past two weeks and are picking up now,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>Another market maker noted Zeneca was also underpinned by investors switching into the shares out of SmithKline Beecham Plc.</p>
<p>Shares in SmithKline were 14 pence lower at 1,040-1/2.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
